Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: preserve a pending mailbox request

The coherent mailbox buffer remains valid after a response timeout, but the
next caller immediately overwrites it and reuses the control registers. A
late response can corrupt that request or be mistaken for its completion.

Under the existing core lock, check the current WAIT_RSP/DONE state before
writing either the payload or request registers. Return -EBUSY while the old
request is still pending and propagate read errors. A late completion allows
the next caller to proceed without another busy wait or added software state.

This protects mailbox ownership; it does not cancel a timed out command,
retry it, reset the firmware, or change callers' recovery policy.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -191,6 +191,15 @@
 	 */
 	spin_lock_bh(&core->lock);
 
+	/* A timeout does not cancel the previous request or its DMA access. */
+	ret = regmap_read(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(3) + offset, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		goto unlock;
+	if ((val & (MBOX_MSG_WAIT_RSP | MBOX_MSG_DONE)) == MBOX_MSG_WAIT_RSP) {
+		ret = -EBUSY;
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
 	memcpy(core->buf, data, len);
 
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(0) + offset, core->addr);
@@ -210,7 +219,7 @@
 	/* Copy the trailing reply_len bytes of the response. */
 	if (!ret && reply)
 		memcpy(reply, core->buf + len - reply_len, reply_len);
-
+unlock:
 	spin_unlock_bh(&core->lock);
 
 	return ret;
